  "date": "2026-11-18",
  "title": "The shape obstacle was a parsing artifact: of real single-line CODE edits, 81.3% need only a single in-vocabulary expression and 86.1% are addressable by the existing machinery; statement-form repairs are 8.7%, not 51.4%",
  "corrects": {
    "file": "canonical/verification/WHAT_A_REAL_FIX_NEEDS_FROM_THE_SITE_20261118_V1.json",
    "published_claim": "\"The insufficiency is SHAPE: half of real single-line edits are not a single expression replacement\" -- therefore the next build should be statement-level repair.",
    "what_was_actually_true": "Of the 118 edits called \"not a single expression\", 26 were not code at all (comments and docstrings) and 71 were code split across lines -- an artifact of diffing LINE PAIRS. Resolving those at statement level leaves 18 statement-form changes in 241 edits (7.5%). The published conclusion would have sent the next build at 7.5% of the population while the real obstacle -- identification -- was already measured and unaddressed.",
    "the_defect": "A line-pair diff cannot see code that spans lines; a SyntaxError on a line was treated as \"not an expression change\" instead of \"this instrument cannot see this edit\"."
  },
  "numbers_corrected": {
    "single_line_edits_examined": 241,
    "not_code_comment_or_docstring": 33,
    "code_edits": 208,
    "single_expression_in_vocabulary": 169,
    "single_expression_in_vocabulary_of_code_edits": 0.8125,
    "two_expression_joint_addressable": 10,
    "addressable_by_existing_machinery_of_code_edits": 0.8606,
    "statement_form": 18,
    "statement_form_of_code_edits": 0.0865,
    "too_large": 9,
    "needs_new_name": 1,
    "unresolved_continuation": 1,
    "raw_totals": {
      "NOT_CODE__COMMENT_OR_DOCSTRING": 33,
      "SINGLE_EXPRESSION__IN_VOCABULARY": 169,
      "TWO_EXPRESSIONS__JOINT_ADDRESSABLE": 10,
      "STATEMENT_FORM__NOT_AN_EXPRESSION": 18,
      "TOO_LARGE": 9,
      "NEEDS_NEW_NAME": 1,
      "CONTINUATION__CODE_SPLIT_ACROSS_LINES": 1
    }
  },
  "what_this_means": "For real single-line code edits, expressiveness is NOT the binding constraint: the repair form this project already has -- one or two expressions over names in scope -- is addressable on 86.1% of them by necessary condition. What remains is evidence: whether the observations available on a task separate the surviving candidates. That is the previous build's 1-4 chosen queries, and it is the only place left to work.",
  "the_three_instrument_defects_in_this_series": [
    "shallowest-instead-of-deepest AST change point: reported 100% NOT_SINGLE_EXPRESSION",
    "ancestors counted as independent change points: reported every edit as two or more changes",
    "line-pair diffing: reported 51.4% \"shape\" where the truth is 7.5%"
  ],
  "what_in_vocabulary_means": "A NECESSARY condition, not sufficiency: every free name of the new expression is in scope at the site in the parent version, the expression is within the enumerator node budget, and exactly one expression subtree changed. Reachability also needs the grammar to generate that form, which the enumerator covers for the operators, subscripts, attributes and calls it implements; this measurement does not execute the site, so it cannot confirm generation for a specific case.",
